# {{.Name}} ({{.Type}})

Creates and manages a long-lived S3-compatible [object storage](https://www.latitude.sh/dashboard) access key.

The API returns the secret **only once**, at creation. By default it is kept in the Terraform state as a sensitive value; set `pgp_key` to keep only a PGP-encrypted copy in state instead (the plaintext never touches the state). There is no update endpoint, so changing any attribute forces a new resource — which rotates the credentials (`terraform apply -replace=...` rotates on demand).

For a run-scoped key that never persists anywhere, use the `latitudesh_object_storage_access_key` [ephemeral resource](../ephemeral-resources/object_storage_access_key) instead.

~> Because the secret cannot be retrieved after creation, this resource does not support `terraform import`.

